  "Question": "There are \\(2\\) boys for every \\(3\\) girls in Ms. Johnson’s math class. If there are \\(30\\) students in her class, what percent of them are boys?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(20\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(40\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(60\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(66\\dfrac{2}{3}\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The ratio gives \\(2\\) parts boys and \\(3\\) parts girls, so the whole class has \\(2+3=5\\) equal parts. Therefore the fraction of students who are boys is\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{40}{100}=40\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(40\\%\\), choice C.",
